## Key Learnings

* Detection reliability depends on telemetry integrity; attackers may target logging systems before detection logic
* Baselining systems are vulnerable to slow poisoning and require bounded, auditable updates
* Rule stores and suppression configurations are high-value targets and need strict governance + rollback
* SOC pipelines must monitor themselves; missing telemetry is a security incident signal, not just ops noise

